# The Server image builds from the repo root (see Server/Serval.Server/Dockerfile), so this file
# — not the one inside Server/Serval.Server/ — is what governs the build context.

# Build output and local state. Never ship these into the image. Scoped to Server/ and Shared/
# specifically: App/serval_app has its own lib/data, lib/models, lib/media — ordinary Dart source
# folders, not build output — which a bare **/data/ etc. would silently drop from the build
# context (as happened: undefined-symbol errors for types that live in lib/data).
Server/**/bin/
Server/**/obj/
Server/**/media/
Server/**/data/
Shared/**/bin/
Shared/**/obj/
**/*.user
**/appsettings.*.local.json

# Model weights: 3.3 GB that are mounted as a volume at runtime, never baked in. Without this
# every build would upload them to the daemon before doing anything.
Server/**/models/

# CameraModule is a separate linux-arm64 deployment the Server image does not build. The one
# exception is the vendored Silero VAD (2.3 MB, version-pinned in git), which the image carries
# as a seed so /app/fetch-models.sh can populate a models volume without a repo checkout.
CameraModule/
!CameraModule/Serval.CameraModule/models/silero_vad.onnx

# App/serval_app IS built into the Server image now (its web build ends up in wwwroot — see
# Server/Serval.Server/Dockerfile), so only its build output is excluded, not the source itself.
App/serval_app/build/
App/serval_app/.dart_tool/
App/serval_app/linux/flutter/ephemeral/

# Test projects: not published, and excluding them keeps them out of the restore graph.
Server/Serval.Server.Tests/
Shared/Serval.Ai.Tests/

# VCS, IDE, OS cruft.
.git/
.github/
**/.claude/
**/.vs/
**/.idea/
**/.DS_Store
